      "paragraph_id": "the-old-capital-p00117",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "真一领头踏上了池子的踏石。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Shinichi led the way onto the stepping stones in the pond.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "the-old-capital-p00117",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "这叫作“涉水”。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "This was called \"wading across.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "the-old-capital-p00117",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "这是一种圆踏石，就像把华表切断排列起来似的。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "They were a kind of round stepping stone, as if ornamental pillars had been cut into sections and lined up.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "the-old-capital-p00117",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "千重子踏上去，有时还得稍稍撩起和服的下摆。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When Chieko stepped onto them, she sometimes had to lift the hem of her kimono a little.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
